// Title: UAC Bypass Using Windows Media Player - Registry
// Sigma ID: 5f9db380-ea57-4d1e-beab-8a2d33397e93
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Christian Burkard (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-08-23 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1548.002
// Description: Detects the pattern of UAC Bypass using Windows Media Player osksupport.dll (UACMe 32)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/hfiref0x/UACME
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_uac_bypass_wmp.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\AppCompatFlags\\Compatibility Assistant\\Store\\C:\\Program Files\\Windows Media Player\\osk.exe" and RegistryValueData =~ "Binary Data"
